/* A closed query with two positive predicate occurrences and no negative
   one, so MuCyc solves the negated query [not P 0 /\ not P 1] (CHC-shaped)
   and flips its verdict.  Valid: P holds at every even non-negative
   integer, so P 0 holds.  Twin: positive_disjunction_flip_invalid.hes. */
P 0 \/ P 1
s.t.
P (x: int): bool =mu x = 0 \/ (x > 0 /\ P (x - 2));
